{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01TtnYFPZeADyCyzf6RQmkaj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now let me save the current measurements. Let me also look at the nsight data for the current state.\n\nCurrent measurements (after the first optimization):\n\n| Config | STARK excl trace | Constraints | Round 0 | LogUp GKR | MLE Rounds | Openings | WHIR | Stacked Reduction | Trace Commit |\n|--------|-----------------|-------------|---------|-----------|------------|----------|------|-------------------|--------------|\n| APC 0  | 2171ms          | 1311ms      | 173ms   | 1016ms    | 118ms      | 334ms    | 218ms| 113ms             | 521ms        |\n\n\n| APC 100| 2077ms          | 1316ms      | 381ms   | 782ms     | 149ms      | 340ms    | 137ms| 203ms             | 419ms        |\n| APC 300| 2358ms          | 1541ms      | 569ms   | 791ms     | 180ms      | 412ms    | 100ms| 310ms             | 403ms        |\n\nI'm comparing the performance across different APC configurations to see how the timing changes as I increase the parameter values. Looking at the performance breakdown across different APC configurations, I'm noticing that while STARK improved from a 1.153 ratio down to 1.086, the underlying work metrics are decreasing much more dramatically—cells dropped by 2.3x, yet STARK's execution time barely scaled accordingly. This suggests something in the STARK pipeline isn't scaling linearly with the reduction in problem size, which is worth investigating further. Constraint Instances: 505M / 1126M = 0.45x (2.2x reduction)\n- Bus Interaction Messages: 448M / 965M = 0.46x (2.2x reduction)\n\nBut STARK excl trace: 2358 / 2171 = 1.09x (actually INCREASES)\n\nThe components:\n- Round 0: 569/173 = 3.3x INCREASE (bad scaling)\n- LogUp GKR: 791/1016 = 0.78x (decreases, but only 1.3x)\n- MLE Rounds: 180/118 = 1.5x INCREASE\n- Stacked Reduction: 310/113 = 2.7x INCREASE (bad scaling)\n- WHIR: 100/218 = 0.46x (scales well)\n- Trace Commit: 403/521 = 0.77x (scales somewhat)\n\nThe scaling bottlenecks are Round 0 with 3.3x slowdown from 623 AIR instances versus 99, Stacked Reduction jumping from 113ms to 310ms due to many more small traces, and MLE Rounds increasing by 1.5x. The previous optimization helped Round 0 by about 94ms, but the biggest remaining opportunity is Stacked Reduction at 310ms where the degenerate kernel is running thousands of instances with low average cost per call.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2625,"cache_read_input_tokens":54420,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2625},"output_tokens":11,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f8b3f9a5-d318-4292-b8d9-cc11d3b0ac84","uuid":"c285d44d-d19f-4843-8aa2-679118127c12"}
